Subject: Close the color buffers a guest closed last, once their delay has passed

A ColorBuffer whose last reference the guest closes is not destroyed at once: it goes on a
delayed close list, since a guest's gralloc may free a buffer and register it again within
moments. The list was looked at only inside the next closeColorBuffer, which destroyed what had
waited a second or more. Whatever was closed last therefore stayed until some other buffer was
closed. When a video ends, its app's surface lets go of all its buffers within the same second
(a 4K stream's queue holds a dozen or more YUV ColorBuffers of 11 to 17 MiB each), so the whole
batch waited for the next close; with one still app left open (a music player that draws
nothing new), that never came, and the renderer kept the video's buffers. On the owner's PC
(0.2.4-dev) the renderer held about 580 MiB more private memory five minutes after a 4K YouTube
video closed than it did with one app before; this list is where the code keeps the video's
buffers after their last close.

FrameBuffer::closeDelayedColorBuffers now destroys every ColorBuffer on the list whose delay has
passed, under the same locks the close takes, and says how many. The renderer's trim calls it
once a second, so a closed buffer goes one to two seconds after its last close, whether or not
anything closes after it. The delay itself, and what it protects, are unchanged.

diff --git a/host/FrameBuffer.h b/host/FrameBuffer.h
--- a/host/FrameBuffer.h
+++ b/host/FrameBuffer.h
@@ -235,2 +235,10 @@
     void closeColorBuffer(HandleType p_colorbuffer);

+    // Destroys the ColorBuffers whose last reference the guest closed at least the close
+    // delay ago and that nothing opened since. closeColorBuffer does it only for what waited
+    // before it, so the buffers closed last (a whole video's, which go within one second)
+    // otherwise stayed until another buffer was closed. Returns how many were destroyed. An
+    // embedder calls it now and then.
+    int closeDelayedColorBuffers();
+
     // Destroy a Buffer created previously. |p_buffer| is its handle value as
diff --git a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
--- a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
+++ b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
@@ -1386,3 +1386,26 @@
 }

+int FrameBuffer::closeDelayedColorBuffers() {
+    // With the guest's reference count pipe the guest destroys its buffers itself, and the
+    // list is never filled.
+    if (m_refCountPipeEnabled) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    AutoLock mutex(m_lock);
+    size_t before = 0;
+    {
+        AutoLock colorBufferMapLock(m_colorBufferMapLock);
+        if (m_colorBufferDelayedCloseList.empty()) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        before = m_colorbuffers.size();
+    }
+    performDelayedColorBufferCloseLocked(false);
+    AutoLock colorBufferMapLock(m_colorBufferMapLock);
+    const size_t after = m_colorbuffers.size();
+    return after < before ? static_cast<int>(before - after) : 0;
+}
